            <ArticleTitle>[Aorto-coronary and mammary-coronary bypass of the working heart without extracorporeal circulation in patients with ischemic heart disease and a history of two or more myocardial infarctions].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>9-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The paper shows how successfully surgical myocardial revascularization can be performed on the working heart without applying extracorporeal circulation in 17 patients with a history of two or more myocardial infarctions. Deaths were not observed among the patients operated on. The follow-ups of the patients were 1-2 months.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
